@startuml
title find_me_in_wood — LNP/3: one handshake agrees the set, switching within it is instant
autonumber
participant "A" as A
participant "B" as B

== 1. Handshake once (inside encrypted, signed beacons) ==
A ->> B : beacon {offers=[BT, WD, SMS(+380..A)]}
B ->> A : beacon {offers=[BT, WD, SMS(+380..B)], acks=[A: h]}
A ->> B : beacon {acks=[B: h]}
note over A, B : same hash on both sides -> set {BT, WD, SMS} agreed;\nboth start on the cheapest: BT

== 2. Switch within the agreed set: no handshake ==
A -> A : user: link to B -> SMS (applies at once)
A ->> B : beacon {sel=[B: SMS, e=1]} (repeated 3x; may be relayed)
B -> B : SMS in agreed set, e newer -> link(A)=SMS (no answer)
A ->> B : SMS "FMIW1:..." position report (every 30 min, max 10/h)

== 3. Quiet link: suggestion only ==
note over A : no beacon from B on the selected link\n-> member list: "Bluetooth quiet — use Wi-Fi Direct?"\nnothing switches unless the user taps
@enduml
